  "info": {
    "title": "Warehouse with forklifts (floor plan)",
    "category": "Logistics",
    "description": "A small warehouse on a real-metre floor plan: pallets are unloaded at the dock, driven by forklift to one of two storage zones, driven again to picking, and leave on a take-away conveyor to shipping. Travel time is geometry -- distance along the aisle network divided by the forklift speed -- so moving the dock or adding a truck changes the KPIs the way hand reasoning says it should.",
    "author": "Naga",
    "notes": "Distances in metres, times in minutes, speeds in metres per minute (50 m/min loaded is about 0.8 m/s, a cautious indoor forklift; the belt runs at 12 m/min). Fast movers are stored close to the dock, bulk pallets far away, so the two routings really do cost different amounts of driving."
  },
